#     description: "Archived release (all versions)"
abstract: >
  A research platform for pothole detection that trains and fairly
  benchmarks image models (YOLOv8, Faster R-CNN, U-Net, ResNet18),
  motion-sensor models (Random Forest, 1D-CNN, BiLSTM), and hybrid
  fusion models, under a strict pothole-versus-other-road-anomaly task
  definition. Includes a 94-test benchmark campaign and a
  pre-registered, blinded real-world transfer study on iPhone and
  nuScenes drives showing that the in-distribution hybrid fusion
  advantage does not survive platform transfer when one modality
  collapses. Ships pre-trained models and a privacy-scrubbed dataset of
  real driving sensor data with human-labeled event clips.
keywords:
  - pothole detection
  - sensor fusion
  - multimodal machine learning
  - domain transfer
  - distribution shift
  - autonomous vehicles
  - computer vision
  - accelerometer
  - road maintenance
  - open dataset
